{"id":"reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named","date":"2026-10-21","topic":"code","region":"world","headline":"Why Linus Torvalds Named His Software Git","source":{"name":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Git"},"accent":"us","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"Linus Torvalds made a new computer program in 2005.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t1-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":4.41,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t1-0.m4a","durJa":5.69,"times":[0.0,0.56,1.36,1.54,1.7,1.88,2.28,2.84,3.18]},{"text":"He gave his work the short name Git.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t1-1.m4a","roles":["S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":2.24,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t1-1.m4a","durJa":4.9,"times":[0.0,0.04,0.18,0.36,0.56,0.86,1.1,1.38]},{"text":"In British English, a git means a bad person.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t1-2.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":3.34,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t1-2.m4a","durJa":4.24,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.28,1.12,1.16,1.48,1.96,2.24,2.58]},{"text":"Torvalds laughed about the name of his program.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t1-3.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":2.41,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t1-3.m4a","durJa":3.64,"times":[0.0,0.5,0.76,1.12,1.3,1.46,1.62,1.72]},{"text":"He said that he names everything after himself.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t1-4.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","S","V","O","M","M"],"dur":2.88,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t1-4.m4a","durJa":4.42,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.2,0.4,0.64,0.9,1.4,1.82]}],"bands":{"core1000":92,"core1800":0,"ngsl":0,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":8},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"gave his work the short name Git.","title":"Double Object Verb Pattern","note":"The verb 'give' can take two objects: the indirect object receiving something (his work) and the direct object being given (the short name Git). This structure shows who receives what without using a preposition like 'to'."},{"i":4,"focus":"names everything after himself","title":"Reflexive Pronouns","note":"Reflexive pronouns like 'himself' are used when the subject and object refer to the same person. Here, it shows that Linus names objects after his own persona."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"Software builder Linus Torvalds created a computer system in 2005.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-0.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":5.55,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-0.m4a","durJa":6.47,"times":[0.0,0.42,1.0,1.62,2.42,2.78,3.16,3.5,4.02,4.32]},{"text":"He named it Git, but this choice surprised many people.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-1.m4a","roles":["S","V","O","C","M","S","S","V","O","O"],"dur":3.76,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-1.m4a","durJa":5.98,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.26,0.48,1.46,1.74,1.94,2.22,2.64,3.1]},{"text":"The word git is British slang for a bad or foolish person.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":4.64,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-2.m4a","durJa":5.4,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.28,0.84,1.42,1.8,2.16,2.56,2.76,3.12,3.42,3.84]},{"text":"People wondered about the strange name, so Torvalds answered with a joke.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-3.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","M","M","M"],"dur":4.55,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-3.m4a","durJa":5.94,"times":[0.22,0.22,0.54,0.92,1.08,1.34,2.48,2.58,3.28,3.58,3.92,4.0]},{"text":"He said that he names all of his projects after himself.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-4.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":3.12,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-4.m4a","durJa":5.35,"times":[0.0,0.04,0.22,0.38,0.56,0.8,1.22,1.42,1.54,1.96,2.52]},{"text":"Today many developers use Git and they will use it for years.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t2-5.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","V","O","M","S","V","V","O","M","M"],"dur":4.67,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t2-5.m4a","durJa":7.06,"times":[0.0,0.22,0.78,1.38,1.86,2.02,2.68,2.8,2.96,3.16,3.34,3.56]}],"bands":{"core1000":88,"core1800":5,"ngsl":0,"tsl":2,"nawl":0,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"named it Git","title":"Object Complement Pattern","note":"Verbs of naming or calling take an object ('it') followed by a noun complement ('Git'). The complement defines what the object is called."},{"i":5,"focus":"will use it for years","title":"Future Tense with Will","note":"The auxiliary verb 'will' forms the simple future tense to express a prediction about future events. It indicates that developers' use of Git will continue over a long period."}]},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"In 2005, developer Linus Torvalds created Git, which is a tool that tracks code changes.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-0.m4a","roles":["M","M","S","S","S","V","O","S","V","C","C","S","V","O","O"],"dur":7.38,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-0.m4a","durJa":8.13,"times":[0.0,0.24,1.66,2.06,2.76,3.54,4.0,4.98,5.06,5.22,5.34,5.58,5.86,6.2,6.56]},{"text":"He needed a fast tool to build Linux, a famous operating system for computers.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-1.m4a","roles":["S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":4.97,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-1.m4a","durJa":8.14,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.3,0.56,0.78,1.24,1.52,1.74,2.62,2.7,3.08,3.46,3.92,4.24]},{"text":"However, the unusual name of the software surprised many people in the technology world.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-2.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":5.58,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-2.m4a","durJa":6.54,"times":[0.0,0.78,0.88,1.3,1.98,2.14,2.26,2.66,3.16,3.82,4.3,4.46,4.54,4.78]},{"text":"In British English slang, a git is an annoying or unpleasant person.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-3.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","S","S","V","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":4.9,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-3.m4a","durJa":5.16,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.4,0.8,1.88,1.94,2.26,2.8,2.92,3.24,3.7,4.22]},{"text":"When people asked about the title, Torvalds offered a funny explanation for his choice.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-4.m4a","roles":["M","S","V","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":4.9,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-4.m4a","durJa":7.0,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.34,0.68,0.98,1.12,1.92,2.42,2.62,2.92,3.18,3.74,4.2,4.32]},{"text":"He joked that he has named all his major software projects after himself.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-5.m4a","roles":["S","V","M","S","V","V","O","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":3.87,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-5.m4a","durJa":6.47,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.3,0.58,0.76,0.9,1.1,1.5,1.72,1.98,2.38,2.92,3.26]},{"text":"Today, millions of software developers have used Git to manage their daily work.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t3-6.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","S","V","V","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":5.23,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t3-6.m4a","durJa":7.7,"times":[0.0,0.62,1.1,1.38,1.62,2.12,2.52,2.78,3.1,3.46,3.7,4.04,4.26]}],"bands":{"core1000":78,"core1800":13,"ngsl":1,"tsl":5,"nawl":0,"beyond":3},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"which is a tool that tracks code changes","title":"Stacked Relative Clauses","note":"This sentence connects two relative clauses using 'which' and 'that'. The pronoun 'which' provides extra descriptive context about Git, while 'that' specifies the function of the tool."},{"i":6,"focus":"have used Git","title":"Present Perfect Tense","note":"The present perfect tense 'have used' connects an action originating in the past with current status. It emphasizes the ongoing relevance and accumulated experience of developers using Git today."}]},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"In April 2005, programmer Linus Torvalds began designing Git, a version control system for tracking software updates.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-0.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":9.16,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-0.m4a","durJa":11.49,"times":[0.0,0.22,0.62,2.06,2.52,3.28,4.08,4.4,5.02,5.98,6.04,6.24,6.56,7.18,7.5,7.78,8.32]},{"text":"Version control software allows large teams of developers to collaborate effectively on complex digital projects.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-1.m4a","roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":7.17,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-1.m4a","durJa":9.04,"times":[0.0,0.28,0.56,1.2,1.68,2.08,2.58,2.84,3.2,3.64,4.02,4.84,5.32,5.82,6.26]},{"text":"Torvalds urgently needed a modern tool to manage the underlying code for the Linux operating system.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-2.m4a","roles":["S","M","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":6.15,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-2.m4a","durJa":8.7,"times":[0.0,0.5,0.88,1.36,1.62,1.94,2.42,2.72,3.0,3.3,3.66,4.24,4.54,4.66,4.86,5.4]},{"text":"Although the new program functioned well, its peculiar title generated widespread confusion among technology workers.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-3.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":7.34,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-3.m4a","durJa":8.39,"times":[0.0,0.2,0.4,0.54,0.84,1.56,2.36,2.44,2.88,3.52,4.12,4.66,5.56,6.08,6.3]},{"text":"In British English vernacular, the word git is commonly used as a mild insult for an annoying individual.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-4.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","S","S","S","V","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":6.98,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-4.m4a","durJa":7.98,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.4,0.68,1.82,1.94,2.14,2.64,3.16,3.58,4.0,4.3,4.4,4.7,5.24,5.62,5.78,6.04]},{"text":"When questioned about his unusual decision, Torvalds humorously reported that he names all his projects after himself.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-5.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","S","M","V","M","S","V","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":7.23,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-5.m4a","durJa":8.81,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.5,0.82,1.0,1.34,2.7,3.1,3.84,4.16,4.56,4.76,4.98,5.4,5.64,5.98,6.42]},{"text":"He lightheartedly implied that his own personality matched the description of the British insult.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-6.m4a","roles":["S","M","V","M","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":4.84,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-6.m4a","durJa":6.63,"times":[0.0,0.02,0.58,1.06,1.32,1.48,1.72,2.18,2.86,3.18,3.48,3.82,3.92,4.12]},{"text":"Today, Git is widely recognized as the standard version control tool relied upon by software engineers everywhere.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t4-7.m4a","roles":["M","S","V","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":7.62,"voiceJa":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/ja/t4-7.m4a","durJa":9.05,"times":[0.0,0.74,0.96,1.24,1.56,2.1,2.56,2.74,3.2,3.5,3.84,4.4,4.66,5.12,5.36,5.62,6.12]}],"bands":{"core1000":67,"core1800":13,"ngsl":6,"tsl":5,"nawl":1,"beyond":8},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"allows large teams of developers to collaborate","title":"Verb + Object + Infinitive","note":"The structure 'allow + object + to-infinitive' indicates enabling someone to perform an action. Here, 'large teams of developers' is the object doing the action expressed by 'to collaborate'."},{"i":3,"focus":"Although the new program functioned well","title":"Concession Clause with Although","note":"The conjunction 'although' introduces a subordinate clause expressing contrast. It sets up an opposing fact before presenting the main clause outcome."}]},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"In April 2005, software engineer Linus Torvalds set out to construct Git, a distributed version control system for tracking source code changes.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-0.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","S","S","S","S","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":10.1,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.22,0.62,1.92,2.26,2.98,3.58,4.16,4.6,4.78,4.92,5.26,6.32,6.44,6.78,7.16,7.52,8.12,8.42,8.7,9.08,9.36]},{"text":"Having previously created the Linux operating system kernel, Torvalds required an exceptionally fast tool to coordinate thousands of parallel development tasks.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-1.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":9.64,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.18,0.58,1.26,1.48,1.72,2.14,2.8,3.68,4.1,4.38,4.76,5.14,5.82,6.3,6.6,6.94,7.6,8.0,8.26,8.92]},{"text":"Existing options failed to satisfy his demanding criteria, prompting him to write an entirely new system in less than two weeks.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-2.m4a","roles":["S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":7.86,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.32,0.58,1.08,1.34,1.82,2.06,2.48,3.74,3.9,4.18,4.32,4.52,4.72,5.16,5.64,6.06,6.4,6.6,6.86,7.12]},{"text":"While the resulting software revolutionized collaborative programming, its peculiar name generated considerable curiosity across the global software development community.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-3.m4a","roles":["M","S","S","S","V","O","O","S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":9.43,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.24,0.52,1.14,2.3,2.64,3.84,3.94,4.32,4.9,5.4,6.02,6.72,7.36,7.6,7.8,8.2,8.6]},{"text":"In British English vernacular, the noun git serves as a colorful insult referring to an unpleasant or obnoxious person.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-4.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":7.39,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.4,0.68,1.82,1.9,2.06,2.6,3.06,3.42,3.5,3.84,4.46,4.86,5.2,5.32,5.82,6.28,6.64]},{"text":"When pressed on why he selected such a derogatory term, Torvalds responded with his characteristic self-deprecating humor.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-5.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":6.96,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.14,0.36,0.64,0.92,1.14,1.48,1.82,1.96,2.2,3.42,3.78,4.08,4.4,4.56,5.4,6.36]},{"text":"He famously quipped that he was an egotistical creator who habitually named all of his software projects after himself.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-6.m4a","roles":["S","M","V","M","S","V","C","C","C","S","M","V","O","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":6.12,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.06,0.32,0.86,1.0,1.16,1.3,1.4,2.06,2.54,2.9,3.46,3.76,4.14,4.32,4.44,4.68,5.2,5.52]},{"text":"Nearly two decades later, Git has become the indispensable backbone of modern software engineering, powering major repository platforms worldwide.","voice":"voice/reserve-code-why-linus-torvalds-named/t5-7.m4a","roles":["M","M","M","M","S","V","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":9.14,"voiceJa":null,"durJa":null,"times":[0.0,0.18,0.52,0.86,1.7,1.84,2.06,2.28,2.56,3.04,3.8,4.08,4.3,4.8,5.76,6.14,6.56,6.9,7.66]}],"bands":{"core1000":63,"core1800":14,"ngsl":5,"tsl":5,"nawl":0,"beyond":13},"grammar":[{"i":1,"focus":"Having previously created the Linux operating system kernel","title":"Perfect Participle Clause","note":"A perfect participle clause ('Having + past participle') modifies the main clause subject and highlights an action completed before the main verb took place. Here, it concisely gives background rationale for why Torvalds needed a fast tool."},{"i":2,"focus":"prompting him to write an entirely new system","title":"Present Participle Result Clause","note":"An -ing participle clause at the end of a sentence often expresses the result or consequence of the main clause action. It connects cause and effect smoothly without starting a new sentence."}]}},"glossary":[{"word":"slang","lemma":"slang","pos":"noun","ipa":"/slæŋ/","definition":"Informal words used by a specific group of people.","tiers":["t2","t3"]},{"word":"collaborate","lemma":"collaborate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlæbəˌreɪt/","definition":"To work together with others on a shared project.","tiers":["t4"]},{"word":"insult","lemma":"insult","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɪnsʌlt/","definition":"An offensive or disrespectful remark aimed at someone.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"peculiar","lemma":"peculiar","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/pɪˈkjuːljər/","definition":"Strange, unusual, or unexpected in a surprising way.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"vernacular","lemma":"vernacular","pos":"noun","ipa":"/vərˈnækjələr/","definition":"The informal language spoken by people in a specific region.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"quipped","lemma":"quip","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kwɪpt/","definition":"Made a clever, witty, or humorous remark.","tiers":["t5"]},{"word":"backbone","lemma":"backbone","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbækˌboʊn/",